    "text_delta": " brief 10–15 minute phone call with the HR lead or the panel chair:\n   > *\"I understand the municipality is busy finalizing the appointment, but as someone committed to advancing in municipal leadership, I would greatly appreciate a brief 10-minute phone call to hear any advice the panel might have for my future professional development.\"*\n   \n   Panels are far more candid and responsive over the phone than in writing.\n\n2. **Frame your public-facing skills in future interviews:**\n   Recognize that for Director-level roles, your technical mastery is already established. Emphasize political acumen, crisis management, council relations, and public consultation stories alongside your planning expertise.\n\n3. **Leave the gender composition aside:**\n   Raising the gender makeup of the panel in any follow-up will likely be perceived as confrontational and ungrounded (given that another man was hired), which could close doors with that municipality or within the local planning network.\n",
